title the hardware vision molts into the seed, and the round writes down what its own guards taught
prompt Keaton asked to add the mantrapod, mantrabox, minisforum, cerebras, MMT, WSE, right-to-repair, ecological, recyclable, RAM-only and USB-C-only writings to the seed, molted and reimagined in Gauge Civic TAME; then to tablecloth the round's insights into external research and silo the value into active-designing and active-development.
think Surveyed before molting. The two Mantrapod venture pitches are sub_excluded from the seed, and reading them showed why: three lines of byline naming a coauthor, which is incidental identity rather than identity-as-subject.
think That is the KYRI.md case again, so the same answer applies -- write a depersonalized Gauge mutant at a fresh stamp, ship it, and leave the dated pitches withheld and whole.
think Chose one foundation over many molts. The named terms are one thesis rather than a dozen: a computer that forgets by construction and opens with a screwdriver, with a desk companion where the memory lives.
think Checked MMT against the tree rather than guessing, since it sits beside Cerebras in the list and could have been either. The tree uses it as Modern Monetary Theory -- buyout proposals and budget precedents -- so it is the civic financing thread.
think Bounded the Cerebras claim carefully. The tree already cites WSE SRAM as the teacher for on-wafer memory, so the page studies the arrangement as a concept, states that every line of code here is ours, and leaves any claim about their current products to them. Wrote CS series rather than naming a model I cannot verify.
think Named the cost beside every gain rather than pitching four wins. A cable-only device asks something real of someone who cannot easily attach one, and that stands as an open design question rather than a solved one.
think For the insights, wrote three pieces to three rooms by the design-rooms test. External research carries what generalizes past this tree. Active-designing carries the durable finding about how a guard is designed. Active-development carries the round record, which is worth little with the code deleted.
think The finding worth the most: four of the five faults this day were EDGES rather than defects -- every guard behaved exactly as written, about a narrower subject than it appeared to cover. Testing finds defects; only use finds edges.
think Drew the six dimensions out of the four edges -- content, location, time, mode, visibility, reach -- and was honest that the list came from faults rather than foresight, so it is a prompt rather than a taxonomy.
obs Three of this round's faults were mine and same-day, and an instrument caught all three ahead of review. That is the argument for building guards while moving fast rather than after.
obs Four separate repairs this round were this session's own earlier renames arriving late in living prose. A breach rename finishes when the guards go green AND the prose stops saying the old name, and those land on different days.
